# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF on
# every platform, so a Windows working tree and a Linux CI runner produce the
# same bytes. This fences the class of defect that broke the first CI run: a test
# hashed data/processed/planets_assessed.csv, the stored blob was LF, and
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone had written CRLF into the working tree.
#
# Binary files are excluded from the normaliser. models/radius_model.joblib is a
# pickled model whose digest is pinned in tests/test_ml_predict.py, so a single
# byte of difference would break the guard.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.joblib binary
*.pkl binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
